lights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6686f71b45b176c9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLooking at state/jurisdiction ... going back to 2003. Among the states/jurisdictions with score declines, <strong>18 scored lower than the national average score for public school students in 2022</strong>; 16 had average scores that were not significantly different from the national ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6686f71b45b176c9\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9f41f7c2a2f19597\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9f41f7c2a2f19597\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0cea709100c93bef\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAVERAGE SCORES FOR STATE/JURISDICTION AND THE NATION (PUBLIC)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0cea709100c93bef\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"61b44d71127c36df\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOVEMBER 2022\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"61b44d71127c36df\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://csgsouth.org/wp-content/uploads/QofM-November.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"94558651a0b2aeed\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLastly, for the eighth-grade reading assessment, no Southern state scored above the national average (260) but five · states – Florida (260), Georgia (260), <strong>Kentucky (258),</strong> Tennessee (258), and Virginia (260) – did score on par with the ... TABLE 1. COMPARISON OF CSG SOUTH STATE SCORES ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"94558651a0b2aeed\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"csgsouth.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fefdf2116cee0f85\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe Nation's Report Card | NAEP\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fefdf2116cee0f85\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bdac6d80e6ae02d2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP is an educational assessment. Often called The Nation&#x27;s Report Card, it provides national, state, and district-level results about students&#x27; academic achievement.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bdac6d80e6ae02d2\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 9, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6c787f2144209053\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe New NAEP Scores Highlight a Standards Gap in Many States - FutureEd\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6c787f2144209053\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.future-ed.org/the-new-naep-scores-highlight-a-standards-gap-in-many-states/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"66b95801410e6aaa\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhile state math scores declined dramatically between 2019 and 2022, particularly in eighth grade, only in Arizona, Arkansas, Florida, Idaho, and Vermont in fourth grade and Arkansas, Michigan, and Missouri in eighth grade did state test scores decline between 2022 and 2024. But students returned to pre-pandemic math proficiency levels in few states. And many states that reported large gains in proficiency on either their fourth-grade or eighth-grade state math assessments between 2022 and 2024—including Oklahoma (+8 percentage points), Alaska (+19), New York (+17), and Wisconsin (+22)—lowered the scores on their tests required to earn proficiency ratings.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"66b95801410e6aaa\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 10, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.future-ed.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4d4c4daf2feddbb7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExplore Results for the 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4d4c4daf2feddbb7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4e210e2a08b23370\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2024 Report Card : Grades 4 &amp; 82024 Report Card : Grade 12 ... NOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong> at grades 4 and 8, and ranges from 0 to 300 at grade 12. Accommodations were not permitted in NAEP mathematics assessments prior to 1996 at the national level for grades 4 and 8.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4e210e2a08b23370\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "Nation's Report Card grade 8 math scores 2022 state Kentucky Arizona South Carolina Kansas", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 1031, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2c12cd99dba44e18\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe Nation's Report Card\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2c12cd99dba44e18\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0b8048b3587dcf30\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nFind key data for state/jurisdiction performance on the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) assessments in mathematics, reading, writing, and science at grades 4, 8 and 12 (where applicable).\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0b8048b3587dcf30\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cee505d8ef3180