{"type": "message", "id": "e5acd07d", "parentId": "68a1f35c", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T10:57:40.361Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "toolu_bdrk_01Rdij1BdS4eDdXM21FvyYG7", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"2022 NAEP mathematics grade 8 state scores Kentucky Arizona South Carolina Kansas 270\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 947,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9dd84575daad1e16\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9dd84575daad1e16\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"44a799d6574c338e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, <strong>the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"44a799d6574c338e\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"da5f3d29ebd5a52a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT KENTUCKY  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"da5f3d29ebd5a52a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KY8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"31a63628c79a5639\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: <strong>The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"31a63628c79a5639\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e60542dbb05281b3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP About - 2022 FPE Mathematics Grade 8 State\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e60542dbb05281b3\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/about/2022fpeg8mathstate.aspx\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"985c91cab2e1e2ad\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExplore NAEP results! By clicking &quot;continue&quot; you will be leaving the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) operational website and opening The Nation&#x27;s Report Card (NRC) website. Explore NAEP results about students&#x27; performance, and access a suite of data tools\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"985c91cab2e1e2ad\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"July 31, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"102d404ce3c13f69\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: Mathematics Highlights 2022\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"102d404ce3c13f69\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c3364a08228c17bc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe average eighth-grade mathematics ... compared to 2019. Average scores are reported on NAEP mathematics scales at grades 4 and 8 that range from <strong>0 to 500</strong>....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c3364a08228c17bc\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d3817aa92673b637\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d3817aa92673b637\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"15430c89bd8c2a1e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: <strong>The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"15430c89bd8c2a1e\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9c00e66e1c5d1d96\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment: Highlighted Results at Grades 4 and 8 for the Nation, States, and Districts | IES\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9c00e66e1c5d1d96\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/use-work/resource-library/report/statistical-analysis-report/2022-naep-mathematics-assessment-highlighted-results-grades-4-and-8-nation-states-and-districts\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f4e3f0db4012f544\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis report presents selected results from the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) 2022 mathematics assessment. The report includes national, state, and district results on the performance of fourth- and eighth-grade students. Results are presented in terms of average scores and as percentages of students performing at or above the three NAEP achievement levels: NAEP Basic, NAEP Proficient, and NAEP Advanced.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f4e3f0db4012f544\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a269d31a445ab818\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a269d31a445ab818\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f98288b37392697a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhile average scores decreased between 2019 and 2022 for almost all student groups nationally, this overall pattern differed across the states. Compared to 2019, female students scored lower in 38 states in 2022, whereas male fourth-graders scored lower in 26 states.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f98288b37392697a\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"be05259346480a13\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 National Assessment of Educational Progress Grade 8 Mathematics Results\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"be05259346480a13\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.fldoe.org/core/fileparse.php/7667/urlt/2022NAEPGrade8Math.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ad0854e044ed3bbf\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNational Assessment of Educational Progress · <strong>Grade 8 Mathematics Results</strong>\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ad0854e044ed3bbf\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.fldoe.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d5a261596ab8c3eb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOVEMBER 2022\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d5a261596ab8c3eb\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://csgsouth.org/wp-content/uploads/QofM-November.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9dac7362ae83d0a9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOn October 24, 2022, the United States Department of Education’s National Center for Education Statistics (NCES) · released the results of the National Assessment of Education Progress (NAEP) – commonly referred to as “The Nation’s\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9dac7362ae83d0a9\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"csgsouth.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"79720702049cc1f5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExplore Results for the 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"79720702049cc1f5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"28a15e86556fdabe\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDownload a summary of the 2022 mathematics results. ... More detailed mathematics assessment results are available throughout this Report Card. ... The NAEP mathematics assessment measures students&#x27; knowledge and skills in mathematics and students&#x27; ability to apply their knowledge in problem-solving situations.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"28a15e86556fdabe\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "2022 NAEP mathematics grade 8 state scores Kentucky Arizona South Carolina Kansas 270", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 947, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9dd84575daad1e16\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9dd84575daad1e16\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"44a799d6574c338e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, <strong>the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"44a799d6574c338e\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"da5f3d29ebd5a52a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT KENTUCKY  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"da5f3d29ebd5a52a\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KY8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"31a63628c79a5639\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOTE: <strong>The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"31a63628c79a5639\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e60542dbb05281b3\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP About - 2022 FPE Mathematics Grade 8 State\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e60542dbb05281b3\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/about/2022fpeg8mathstate.aspx", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"985c91cab2e1e2ad\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nExplore NAEP results! By clicking &quot;continue&quot; you will be leaving the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) operational website and opening The Nation&#x27;s Report Card (NRC) website. Explore NAEP results about students&#x27; performance, and access a suite of data tools\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"985c91cab2e1e2ad\">>>", "published": "July 31, 2023", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"102d404ce3c13f69\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: Mathematics Highlights 2022\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"102d404ce3c13f69\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c3364a08228c17bc\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe average eighth-grade mathematics ... compared to 2019. Average scores are reported on NAEP mathematics scales at grades 4 and 8 that range from <strong>0 to 500</strong>....\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c3364a08228c17bc\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d3817aa92673b637\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d3817aa92673b637\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"15430c89bd8c2a1e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOTE: <strong>The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"15430c89bd8c2a1e\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9c00e66e1c5d1d96\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment: Highlighted Results at Grades 4 and 8 for the Nation, States, and Districts | IES\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9c00e66e1c5d1d96\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/use-work/resource-library/report/statistical-analysis-report/2022-naep-mathematics-assessment-highlighted-results-grades-4-and-8-nation-states-and-districts", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f4e3f0db4012f544\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThis report presents selected results from the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) 2022 mathematics assessment. The report includes national, state, and district results on the performance of fourth- and eighth-grade students. Results are presented in terms of average scores and as percentages of students performing at or above the three NAEP achievement levels: NAEP Basic, NAEP Proficient, and NAEP Advanced.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f4e3f0db4012f544\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a269d31a445ab818\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Gr